# ============================================================================
# Shared-edge mode. Copy to /opt/solutionmines/edge.env ONLY when this box
# runs more than one site behind a single proxy that is not ours:
#
#   sudo install -d -m 0755 /opt/solutionmines
#   sudo cp deploy/edge.env.example /opt/solutionmines/edge.env
#   sudo chmod 600 /opt/solutionmines/edge.env
#
# The moment the file exists, bootstrap.sh, bring-up.sh and deploy.sh treat
# the box as shared: no nginx, no certificates, no firewall changes, no Docker
# install. They also REFUSE to run until all five keys below are set, because
# none of them has a safe default on somebody else's proxy. Everything here is
# commented out, so an unedited copy is refused, never half-used.
#
# The rules (deploy/guard.sh, sm_check_edge_env, enforces them):
#   UPSTREAM_FILE    absolute path, in a directory that already exists and
#                    holds nothing else of the proxy's. NOT in a directory the
#                    proxy loads whole (/etc/nginx/conf.d, sites-enabled,
#                    sites-available, or anything a Caddyfile imports with a
#                    glob such as `import sites/*.caddy`): a bare upstream
#                    line there breaks the other site's config. This site's
#                    block imports the file by its exact path instead. That
#                    directory, and every one above it, root-owned and not
#                    writable by group or others: deploy.sh writes there as
#                    root. If the file exists, it holds exactly the line for
#                    blue or green (create it that way, before the block).
#   UPSTREAM_LINE    the one line deploy.sh writes into it. Must contain
#                    __COLOUR__ (blue|green) or __PORT__ (3001|3002).
#   EDGE_TEST_CMD    validates the proxy config. A failed test puts the old
#                    upstream file back (or removes it) before any reload.
#   EDGE_RELOAD_CMD  reloads the proxy gracefully.
#   SMOKE_URL        http(s) URL through the proxy, by a HOSTNAME this site's
#                    block matches. Not 127.0.0.1 and not plain localhost: the
#                    proxy routes by Host, so those reach its catch-all. Not
#                    port 3001/3002 either: that is the container itself. A
#                    local alias such as sm.localhost in the site block works
#                    before DNS does. deploy.sh requires the response to report
#                    the commit it just deployed, so a catch-all's empty 200
#                    can no longer pass.
#
# The file is sourced by deploy.sh as root: keep it, and its directory,
# root-owned and not writable by group or others (refused otherwise).
#
# deploy.sh replaces UPSTREAM_FILE by a rename (owner and mode are kept, the
# inode is new), so a proxy in a container must mount the DIRECTORY that
# holds it, never the single file: a single-file bind mount keeps showing the
# old inode.
#
# Before the first deploy, also:
#   - put this site's block in the proxy (docs/03-deployment.md has one for
#     Caddy and one for nginx), and
#   - if the proxy runs in a container, connect it to the shared network:
#       sudo docker network connect edge <proxy-container>
# ============================================================================

# --- Example A: a shared Caddy, itself running in a container --------------
# The proxy reaches the containers by NAME over the `edge` docker network, so
# the switch rewrites a container name rather than a port. /opt/edge on the
# host is mounted at /etc/caddy in the container in this example; the
# Caddyfile's `import sites/*.caddy` does NOT match /opt/edge/upstreams/.
#
# UPSTREAM_FILE=/opt/edge/upstreams/solutionmines.caddy
# UPSTREAM_LINE='reverse_proxy solutionmines-__COLOUR__:3000'
# EDGE_TEST_CMD='docker exec edge-caddy-1 caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile --adapter caddyfile'
# EDGE_RELOAD_CMD='docker exec edge-caddy-1 caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile --adapter caddyfile'
# SMOKE_URL=http://sm.localhost/api/health

# --- Example B: another site's nginx, on the host ---------------------------
# nginx reaches the app on the 127.0.0.1 ports the compose file publishes.
# /etc/nginx/solutionmines/ is a directory of its own (create it first); this
# site's server block uses `upstream solutionmines_app { include
# /etc/nginx/solutionmines/upstream.conf; }`.
#
# UPSTREAM_FILE=/etc/nginx/solutionmines/upstream.conf
# UPSTREAM_LINE='server 127.0.0.1:__PORT__;'
# EDGE_TEST_CMD='nginx -t'
# EDGE_RELOAD_CMD='nginx -s reload'
# SMOKE_URL=http://sm.localhost/api/health
